# Kabyle date words that are also frequent ordinary words.  Alone, with no
# time cue beside them, they take the ordinary sense.
#
# tafsut "spring" is also a girl's given name.  Tatoeba kab 8420141:
# "Sɛant yessetma-tsent tiyaḍ d takniwin Tafsut d Tilelli"; 8420836:
# "06/01/2017 lulent-d Tafsut d Tilelli."  Season sense, 7154718: "Tafsut
# tattawi-d ciṭṭ n leḥmu mi tεedda tegrest qessiḥen."
tafsut
# lḥedd "Sunday" is also "limit".  Tatoeba kab 7209735: "Taẓuri imir tella
# tewweḍ lḥedd-is."; 7151638: "... i εewwleɣ ad geɣ lḥedd i weεraq ...".
# "ass n lḥedd" and "lḥedd-agi" keep the date sense through the cue before or
# after the word.
lḥedd
# azal "daytime, noon" is also "value, worth".  Tatoeba kab 2791855:
# "Tamrint-a ɣur-s azal meqqren."; 2294744: "Ɣur-i azal n yedrimen swayes
# ara t-id-aɣeɣ."  Daytime sense, 7013385: "Ass n lḥedd ɣef ttnac n uzal".
azal
# The CLDR month abbreviations (month_*.voc) are short and read as a month only
# next to a cue: "20 Tub 2023".
yen
fur
meɣ
yeb
may
yun
yul
ɣuc
cte
tub
nun
duǧ
